**Type call: Enneagram 7 (7w8, self-preservation), confidence high.** The tiebreaker is two sentences that a Three would invert: "a new joke in a shitty bar feels ten times better than selling out a 3,000 seat" (JRE #2072, Dec 2023) and "my true wildest dreams were to make $65,000 a year playing B-level clubs" (Slate, Oct 2025).

**Thesis:** the persona is bottomless appetite; the driver is a kid who didn't know his family was poor until adulthood, watching a father who has been in Baltimore ~40 years, built the fittings in half the region's Greek diners, and still isn't a citizen. In his best year on *Cum Town* he made $30,000 and put it on a down payment.

